{
  "name": "How to Plan the Perfect Stairway Lighting Layout",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Getting stairway lighting just right involves more than just picking pretty fixtures. It's about safety and aesthetics. First, consider how many lights you'll need to adequately illuminate every step and landing, keeping in mind the IRC actually requires interior stairways to have lighting that illuminates treads and landings. Think about the type of fixtures: do wall sconces, recessed lights, or LED strip/riser lights fit your home's style and your stairway's width best? For instance, narrow stairways often benefit from fixtures that don't project too far. You'll also need to decide where to place fixtures on the stair run to avoid shadows and dim spots. Don't forget those crucial switch controls at both the top and bottom of the stairs, especially if your stairway has a certain number of treads, as local codes often require this for usability and safety. If you're unsure about code compliance or the best layout, bringing in an expert can make a huge difference in achieving a well-lit and safe stairway.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
